<div class="practice-page">
  <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to exercises</a>
  <h1 class="practice-title">Horizontal Slider</h1>
  <div class="practice-banner"><ul>
    <li>Click the slider then use <code>sendKeys(Keys.ARROW_RIGHT)</code> to move it</li>
    <li>Set a value directly with JavaScript executor: <code>arguments[0].value = '3'</code></li>
    <li>Assert the displayed number next to the slider updates correctly</li>
  </ul></div>
<div class="example">
  
  <h4 class="subheader">Set the focus on the slider (by clicking on it) and use the arrow keys to move it right and left. Or click and drag the slider with your mouse. It will indicate the value of the slider to the right.</h4>
  <div class="sliderContainer">
    <input type="range" min="0.0" max="5.0" step="0.5" value="0" onchange="showValue(this.value)">
    &nbsp;
    <span id="range">0</span>
  </div>
</div>
<script type="text/javascript">
  function showValue(newValue) { $("#range").html(newValue); }
</script>
</div>
